178
00:14:46.559 --> 00:14:47.552
JASON:
I don't know where I am...

179
00:14:48.578 --> 00:14:49.794
or how I got here.

180
00:14:49.795 --> 00:14:52.036
and who those guys were
that wanted to kill me.

181
00:14:52.037 --> 00:14:53.542
But whatever you did
back there was sick.

182
00:14:53.542 --> 00:14:56.008
No. Drunken fist.

183
00:14:57.419 --> 00:15:00.076
Secret kung-fu of the South.

184
00:15:00.077 --> 00:15:02.607
I'm Lu Yan.
traveling scholar.

185
00:15:04.081 --> 00:15:05.426
What land
do you come from. monk?

186
00:15:05.427 --> 00:15:06.579
I'm not a monk.

187
00:15:07.637 --> 00:15:09.334
I'm Jason.

188
00:15:09.335 --> 00:15:11.064
Jason Tripitikas.
from South Boston.

189
00:15:12.827 --> 00:15:14.812
Is this a dream?

190
00:15:14.813 --> 00:15:16.542
No.

191
00:15:16.543 --> 00:15:19.361
Where you came from
is the dream...

192
00:15:19.362 --> 00:15:22.179
through the gate
of no gate.

193
00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:24.806
Is that like a wormhole
or something?

194
00:15:24.807 --> 00:15:26.792
No. It means
you are either a Zen Master...

195
00:15:28.428 --> 00:15:30.027
or you carry something
very special.

196
00:15:30.028 --> 00:15:32.206
This?

197
00:15:32.207 --> 00:15:33.231
It was in a pawn shop.

198
00:15:33.232 --> 00:15:34.352
waiting for a man
to pick it up

199
00:15:34.352 --> 00:15:37.234
and return it
to its rightful owner.

200
00:15:38.549 --> 00:15:39.253
What?

201
00:15:40.727 --> 00:15:43.513
It's long been foretold

202
00:15:43.514 --> 00:15:45.691
that a seeker will come

203
00:15:45.692 --> 00:15:50.208
to return the staff and end
the reign of the Jade Warlord.

204
00:15:50.209 --> 00:15:51.586
Return the staff to who?

205
00:15:52.709 --> 00:15:54.181
The Monkey King.

206
00:15:54.182 --> 00:15:56.871
Born of a stone

207
00:15:56.872 --> 00:16:00.075
on the mountain
of fruit and flowers.

208
00:16:00.076 --> 00:16:02.061
With his weapon in hand.

209
00:16:02.062 --> 00:16:04.911
his Chi became like fire.
[shouting]

210
00:16:04.912 --> 00:16:07.442
his stick fighting
like magic.

211
00:16:07.443 --> 00:16:09.045
He defied the order
of the land...

212
00:16:10.166 --> 00:16:12.280
but the Jade Army
could not defeat him.

213
00:16:19.552 --> 00:16:20.831
MONKEY KING: Ooh!

214
00:16:20.832 --> 00:16:22.114
[soldier screaming]

215
00:16:22.115 --> 00:16:23.107
Hee hee hee hee!

216
00:16:23.108 --> 00:16:24.932
[soldiers shouting]

217
00:16:27.624 --> 00:16:28.264
Aah!
- Aah!

218
00:16:33.102 --> 00:16:35.759
LU: The Monkey King crushed
every soldier sent to stop him.

219
00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:38.611
With his magical staff.
he was unbeatable.

220
00:16:39.829 --> 00:16:41.494
Word of his disobedience

221
00:16:41.495 --> 00:16:44.760
traveled deep
within the Forbidden Kingdom

222
00:16:44.761 --> 00:16:48.508
to the Five Elements Mountain.
land of the immortals.

223
00:16:48.509 --> 00:16:50.847
Once every 500 years.

224
00:16:50.848 --> 00:16:53.507
The Jade Emperor hosts
the Peach Banquet.

225
00:16:53.508 --> 00:16:56.164
It is here.
the Heavenly Ministers gather

226
00:16:56.165 --> 00:16:58.727
to celebrate
their longevity

227
00:16:58.728 --> 00:17:00.777
and drink
the Elixir of Immortality.

228
00:17:02.765 --> 00:17:07.119
One sip of this heavenly brew
will give everlasting life.

229
00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.394
free from mortal suffering
and desire.

230
00:17:11.959 --> 00:17:13.815
[Monkey King laughing]

231
00:17:13.816 --> 00:17:14.841
LU: Into the banquet.

232
00:17:14.842 --> 00:17:17.884
the Monkey King crashed.
uninvited.

233
00:17:17.885 --> 00:17:18.845
MONKEY KING: Whoo!

234
00:17:21.824 --> 00:17:25.571
LU: The Jade Emperor was
enchanted by the Monkey King.

235
00:17:25.572 --> 00:17:28.743
But the Jade Warlord
was not amused.

236
00:17:28.744 --> 00:17:30.376
As Master of the Army.

237
00:17:30.377 --> 00:17:34.124
The Warlord demanded
the Monkey King bow down to him.

238
00:17:34.125 --> 00:17:35.182
[laughing]

239
00:17:37.937 --> 00:17:38.993
[soldiers shouting]

240
00:17:42.646 --> 00:17:45.175
He's a bit unrefined.
that's all.

241
00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:49.756
Give the naughty monkey
a title and let him go.

242
00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:56.899
LU: Satisfied all was well
in heaven and earth.

243
00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:58.469
The Supremely High Emperor

244
00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:01.288
left to begin
his 500 years meditation.

245
00:18:01.289 --> 00:18:05.805
leaving the Jade Warlord
in charge by Mandate of Heaven.

246
00:18:05.806 --> 00:18:08.400
But rather than obey
the Jade Emperor's command.

247
00:18:08.401 --> 00:18:10.866
the Warlord challenged
the Monkey King to a duel.

248
00:18:12.725 --> 00:18:16.376
High atop Five Elements Mountain
in the Warlord's palace.

249
00:18:16.377 --> 00:18:19.323
[drums beating]
the battle of immortals

250
00:18:19.324 --> 00:18:22.206
To prove once and for all
whose skills were supreme.

251
00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.727
[drums grow louder]

252
00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.171
Yah!

253
00:19:12.787 --> 00:19:13.716
[both giggling]

254
00:19:43.219 --> 00:19:44.403
Hmph!

255
00:19:44.404 --> 00:19:44.979
[laughs]

256
00:19:48.376 --> 00:19:52.219
[rumbling]

257
00:20:01.125 --> 00:20:01.829
Huh!

258
00:20:05.034 --> 00:20:06.506
Hwah!

259
00:20:11.343 --> 00:20:12.785
Ohh!

260
00:20:33.063 --> 00:20:34.406
[spears clanging
against staff]

261
00:20:53.436 --> 00:20:55.069
[giggling]

262
00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:58.527
Most excellent stick fighting.
Sun Wukong.

263
00:20:58.528 --> 00:21:01.763
But without your weapon. you're
nothing but a lowly hermit!

264
00:21:01.764 --> 00:21:02.821
Hee!

265
00:21:02.822 --> 00:21:05.062
No more weapons.
no more Chi magic.

266
00:21:06.537 --> 00:21:08.618
Fist against fist.

267
00:21:10.477 --> 00:21:12.430
LU: The Monkey King
was too trusting

268
00:21:12.431 --> 00:21:14.352
and believed
the Warlord's words.

269
00:21:14.353 --> 00:21:15.986
laying down his magic weapon.

270
00:21:15.987 --> 00:21:16.723
[clang]

271
00:21:18.004 --> 00:21:18.645
Hwah!

272
00:21:23.322 --> 00:21:24.571
LU:
Realizing he'd been tricked.

273
00:21:24.572 --> 00:21:26.172
the Monkey King
cast the staff

274
00:21:26.173 --> 00:21:27.422
out into the Middle Kingdom.

275
00:21:42.094 --> 00:21:42.670
Hmm...

276
00:21:45.265 --> 00:21:47.442
martial art
is based on deception...

277
00:21:49.109 --> 00:21:50.197
my friend.

278
00:21:54.042 --> 00:21:54.971
[drum reverberates]

279
00:21:56.349 --> 00:21:57.373
LU: Being immortal.

280
00:21:57.374 --> 00:21:58.846
the Monkey King
could not be killed.

281
00:21:58.847 --> 00:22:00.512
only trapped in stone.

282
00:22:00.513 --> 00:22:02.755
where he waits for the seeker
from the prophesy

283
00:22:02.756 --> 00:22:06.406
to return to him his great
weapon and finally free him.

284
00:22:17.427 --> 00:22:18.899
That's what I heard.
anyway.

285
00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.661
[Chinese lute
playing in background]

286
00:22:20.662 --> 00:22:22.455
Long time ago.

287
00:22:22.456 --> 00:22:24.568
How long
has he been imprisoned?

288
00:22:24.569 --> 00:22:27.964
Five hundred years.
give or take a few decades.

289
00:22:27.965 --> 00:22:30.431
They say
when the Monkey King is free.

290
00:22:30.432 --> 00:22:31.712
the Jade Emperor will return.

291
00:22:34.213 --> 00:22:35.492
How do I get home?

292
00:22:35.493 --> 00:22:39.592
You must return the staff
to Five Elements Mountain.

293
00:22:39.593 --> 00:22:41.130
You must
free the Monkey King.

294
00:22:41.131 --> 00:22:42.668
I can't
free the Monkey King.

295
00:22:42.669 --> 00:22:43.853
I gotta get home.

296
00:22:43.854 --> 00:22:46.256
Innkeeper! More wine.

297
00:22:46.257 --> 00:22:47.536
Jeez. don't you think
you've had one too many?

298
00:22:49.299 --> 00:22:51.445
Wine is my inspiration.

299
00:22:51.446 --> 00:22:53.751
In some parts.
I am known as the poet.

300
00:22:53.752 --> 00:22:54.680
<i>Gambei.</i>

301
00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:01.023
In other parts.
I am known as the beggar.

302
00:23:13.388 --> 00:23:14.381
[speaking Chinese]

303
00:23:17.618 --> 00:23:19.153
[speaking Chinese]

304
00:23:21.076 --> 00:23:23.862
[speaking Chinese]

305
00:23:23.863 --> 00:23:24.823
What do we do now?

306
00:23:24.824 --> 00:23:26.425
How good is your kung-fu?

307
00:23:26.426 --> 00:23:28.219
Ah!

308
00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:29.757
He who speaks does not know.

309
00:23:29.758 --> 00:23:31.871
He who knows
does not speak.

310
00:23:31.872 --> 00:23:32.928
Surely. you are masterful.

311
00:23:39.335 --> 00:23:40.264
Where did you get
that weapon?

312
00:23:40.265 --> 00:23:41.769
It's a fake.

313
00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:44.620
You can find
anything these days

314
00:23:44.621 --> 00:23:46.221
Out of way. old fool.

315
00:23:46.222 --> 00:23:46.959
Huh?

316
00:23:49.778 --> 00:23:50.386
Hand it over.

317
00:23:52.245 --> 00:23:53.077
[playing]

318
00:23:53.078 --> 00:23:55.671
Hand over the weapon...
or die.

319
00:24:02.303 --> 00:24:04.480
[soldiers groaning]

320
00:24:04.481 --> 00:24:05.858
[patrons screaming]

321
00:24:08.261 --> 00:24:08.741
Go!

322
00:24:10.344 --> 00:24:11.688
Whoa!

323
00:24:11.689 --> 00:24:13.097
Whoa! Oh!

324
00:24:14.636 --> 00:24:16.429
Aah! Oh!

325
00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:18.126
[soldiers groaning]

326
00:24:18.127 --> 00:24:19.665
SOLDIER: Hyah!

327
00:24:34.817 --> 00:24:35.937
JASON: Aah!

328
00:24:35.938 --> 00:24:37.283
[groaning]

329
00:24:38.756 --> 00:24:41.351
[Jason gasping]

330
00:24:41.352 --> 00:24:42.344
Lu. help!

331
00:24:43.434 --> 00:24:44.585
[soldiers shouting]

332
00:24:48.238 --> 00:24:50.481
[Jason screaming]

333
00:24:50.482 --> 00:24:51.537
[Lu groaning]

334
00:24:53.076 --> 00:24:54.260
Yaah!

335
00:25:00.796 --> 00:25:02.461
Lu!
Protect yourself!

336
00:25:02.462 --> 00:25:03.134
What?

337
00:25:20.016 --> 00:25:22.033
[Jason shouting]

338
00:25:24.276 --> 00:25:25.589
Yah! Yah!

339
00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:26.165
[clang]
Ohh!

340
00:25:30.202 --> 00:25:30.842
Ayee!

341
00:25:40.997 --> 00:25:41.701
JASON: Whoa!

342
00:25:45.130 --> 00:25:46.185
[groaning]

343
00:25:49.903 --> 00:25:51.150
[shouting]

344
00:25:51.151 --> 00:25:52.720
Whoa!

345
00:26:02.620 --> 00:26:03.740
Hyah!

346
00:26:08.418 --> 00:26:09.410
[officer shouting
command in Chinese]

347
00:26:14.990 --> 00:26:15.918
Let's go!

348
00:26:19.250 --> 00:26:20.146
JASON: Aah!

349
00:26:27.514 --> 00:26:28.794
Oh! Ohhh!

350
00:26:31.902 --> 00:26:32.958
JASON:
Where are you going?

351
00:26:35.297 --> 00:26:36.642
Jump!
- I don't think so!

352
00:26:36.643 --> 00:26:37.794
Don't think! Just do!

353
00:26:39.846 --> 00:26:41.702
[shouting]

354
00:26:41.703 --> 00:26:42.598
[screaming]

355
00:26:46.155 --> 00:26:47.084
[soldiers shouting]

356
00:26:48.461 --> 00:26:49.741
LU: Come on!

357
00:26:49.742 --> 00:26:53.105
Aah!

358
00:26:53.106 --> 00:26:54.002
Ohh!

359
00:26:54.003 --> 00:26:55.538
Aah!

360
00:26:55.539 --> 00:26:57.525
[Lu screaming]

361
00:26:57.526 --> 00:26:58.550
[groaning]

362
00:26:58.551 --> 00:27:00.087
Ah! Thank you!

363
00:27:02.778 --> 00:27:03.931
[officer shouting
in Chinese]

364
00:27:08.287 --> 00:27:09.664
Oh! Such skills. child!

365
00:27:09.665 --> 00:27:11.554
Are you
from Northern Mountains?

366
00:27:11.555 --> 00:27:13.347
She is Golden Sparrow.
from the South.

367
00:27:16.391 --> 00:27:17.672
Yah! Yah!

368
00:27:25.135 --> 00:27:26.480
[soldiers shouting]

369
00:27:38.107 --> 00:27:39.035
[screaming]

370
00:27:40.734 --> 00:27:41.758
[screaming]

371
00:27:53.706 --> 00:27:55.018
Aah!
[horse whinnying]

372
00:28:06.582 --> 00:28:08.439
JASON: You really saved
our lives back there.

373
00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:09.496
I don't know
what we would have done

374
00:28:09.497 --> 00:28:11.033
if you hadn't come along.

375
00:28:11.034 --> 00:28:12.411
She does not think

376
00:28:12.412 --> 00:28:14.301
the drunken immortal
needed his life saved.

377
00:28:15.903 --> 00:28:16.639
You're immortal?

378
00:28:18.017 --> 00:28:19.969
What do you run from.
child?

379
00:28:19.970 --> 00:28:22.116
Bounty hunters
trying to stop her

380
00:28:22.117 --> 00:28:24.294
from reaching
the Five Elements Mountain.

381
00:28:30.540 --> 00:28:32.622
I suggest
you keep riding west

382
00:28:32.623 --> 00:28:34.736
and only stop
to water your horses.

383
00:28:34.737 --> 00:28:35.857
You're not coming?

384
00:28:35.858 --> 00:28:37.618
The journey
to Five Elements Mountain

385
00:28:37.619 --> 00:28:39.444
crosses barrens
and deserts.

386
00:28:39.445 --> 00:28:40.245
Unspeakable dangers.

387
00:28:40.246 --> 00:28:42.166
Worst of all. no wine.

388
00:28:42.167 --> 00:28:43.319
His Elixir.

389
00:28:43.320 --> 00:28:45.178
Every immortal
has one.

390
00:28:45.179 --> 00:28:47.515
I'm very sorry.
Without wine. I would perish.

391
00:28:47.516 --> 00:28:49.245
You must understand this.

392
00:28:49.246 --> 00:28:51.967
No. You must understand this.

393
00:28:51.968 --> 00:28:52.640
This is insane!

394
00:28:54.340 --> 00:28:55.747
You wish to get home?
- Yes.

395
00:28:58.343 --> 00:28:59.110
Then listen well!

396
00:28:59.111 --> 00:29:00.231
If you die here.

397
00:29:00.232 --> 00:29:02.634
you'll be found dead
in the world you left behind.

398
00:29:02.635 --> 00:29:03.627
Do you understand?

399
00:29:06.446 --> 00:29:08.655
My jug is getting low.

400
00:29:08.656 --> 00:29:09.872
I must say goodbye.
Bye-bye.

401
00:29:19.258 --> 00:29:20.250
Lu.

402
00:29:20.251 --> 00:29:22.172
Wait!

403
00:29:22.173 --> 00:29:23.229
Let him go.

404
00:29:23.230 --> 00:29:25.695
You are the one
to return the staff. not him.

405
00:29:27.138 --> 00:29:28.098
How good is your kung-fu?

406
00:29:28.099 --> 00:29:30.436
He's got no kung-fu.

407
00:29:30.437 --> 00:29:32.069
None!

408
00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:33.319
JASON: Lu. wait!

409
00:29:33.320 --> 00:29:35.337
Teach me.

410
00:29:35.338 --> 00:29:36.554
Teach me to fight!

411
00:29:40.559 --> 00:29:41.871
[grunting]

412
00:29:46.515 --> 00:29:48.084
LU:
Swing soft. cut hard!

413
00:29:48.085 --> 00:29:48.789
At the same time!

414
00:29:50.487 --> 00:29:51.479
He's terrible.

415
00:29:56.541 --> 00:29:58.975
I've been your weed-whacker
for two days now

416
00:29:58.976 --> 00:30:01.537
while you sit on your horse
like the King of England.

417
00:30:01.538 --> 00:30:02.529
When are you gonna
teach me kung-fu?

418
00:30:02.530 --> 00:30:04.163
You want to learn kung-fu?

419
00:30:04.164 --> 00:30:05.541
Yeah.

420
00:30:09.513 --> 00:30:10.441
I teach you kung-fu.

421
00:30:13.869 --> 00:30:15.277
Aah!
- That's called strike.

422
00:30:15.278 --> 00:30:17.039
Tomorrow.
I'll teach you block.

423
00:30:17.039 --> 00:30:17.743
Let's go.

424
00:30:19.282 --> 00:30:21.490
LU:
Swing soft. cut hard.

425
00:30:21.491 --> 00:30:22.869
[Jason groaning]

426
00:30:41.735 --> 00:30:43.400
You think you'll teach me
the no shadow kick?

427
00:30:45.514 --> 00:30:47.178
Oh. and the Buddha Palm
technique?

428
00:30:49.614 --> 00:30:51.983
There's a guy
in <i>Virtual Fighter 2</i>

429
00:30:51.984 --> 00:30:53.104
that does
the Buddha Palm technique.

430
00:30:53.105 --> 00:30:54.514
Thanks. Lu.

431
00:30:54.515 --> 00:30:55.699
And he does the. uh...

432
00:30:57.622 --> 00:30:58.069
the Iron Elbow...

433
00:30:59.576 --> 00:31:01.337
And he does
the One-Fingered Death Touch.

434
00:31:01.338 --> 00:31:02.585
The cup's full.

435
00:31:02.586 --> 00:31:03.482
Stop! It's full.

436
00:31:05.436 --> 00:31:07.262
Exactly.

437
00:31:07.262 --> 00:31:09.664
How can you fill your cup
if already full?

438
00:31:09.665 --> 00:31:11.842
How can you learn kung-fu?

439
00:31:11.843 --> 00:31:14.181
You already know so much.

440
00:31:14.182 --> 00:31:15.621
No Shadow Kick.
Buddha Palm!

441
00:31:16.519 --> 00:31:17.639
Empty your cup.

442
00:31:23.374 --> 00:31:25.070
Hopeless.

443
00:31:25.071 --> 00:31:25.679
It is hopeless.

444
00:31:32.854 --> 00:31:35.288
[playing]

445
00:31:46.820 --> 00:31:47.844
It is said that music...

446
00:31:49.606 --> 00:31:53.065
Is a bridge
between earth and heaven.

447
00:31:54.027 --> 00:31:55.019
It's beautiful.

448
00:32:02.227 --> 00:32:03.153
It belonged to her mother.

449
00:32:04.564 --> 00:32:07.479
[thunder]

450
00:32:10.650 --> 00:32:12.378
[thunder]

451
00:32:30.541 --> 00:32:32.878
[thunder]

452
00:32:46.460 --> 00:32:47.355
[speaking Chinese]

453
00:33:29.091 --> 00:33:29.763
[grunting]

454
00:33:44.370 --> 00:33:45.713
[thunder]

455
00:33:55.932 --> 00:33:57.853
[gasp. panting]

456
00:34:02.242 --> 00:34:03.234
Lu Yan?

457
00:34:06.951 --> 00:34:07.398
Lu Yan?

458
00:34:12.523 --> 00:34:13.516
Lu Yan!

459
00:34:15.759 --> 00:34:16.879
Lu Yan!

460
00:34:20.499 --> 00:34:21.203
Sparrow!

461
00:34:41.800 --> 00:34:42.791
[groaning]

462
00:34:55.604 --> 00:34:57.301
[Jason whimpering]

463
00:34:58.615 --> 00:34:59.127
Aah!

464
00:35:05.214 --> 00:35:05.948
GOLDEN SPARROW:
Are you all right?

465
00:35:05.949 --> 00:35:07.422
Jason. what happened?

466
00:35:07.423 --> 00:35:09.440
He took it! The staff!

467
00:35:11.747 --> 00:35:14.180
The Jade Warlord
has sent a bounty hunter.

468
00:35:14.181 --> 00:35:15.398
We are doomed.

469
00:35:17.128 --> 00:35:19.401
[crow caws]

470
00:35:19.402 --> 00:35:21.291
[cawing]

471
00:35:27.089 --> 00:35:27.697
That's his horse.

472
00:35:27.698 --> 00:35:30.548
He must be inside.

473
00:35:30.549 --> 00:35:32.950
Why would he take refuge
in a temple?

474
00:35:32.951 --> 00:35:33.879
Lu: that's what I intend
to find out.

475
00:35:33.880 --> 00:35:35.897
Wait with the horses.

476
00:36:05.782 --> 00:36:07.446
Ah! Good
to get off my feet.

477
00:36:09.625 --> 00:36:10.329
Long day.

478
00:36:11.578 --> 00:36:13.949
So. where are you from?

479
00:36:13.950 --> 00:36:14.620
Shandong Province?

480
00:36:16.672 --> 00:36:18.816
You look like
the Shandong Province type.

481
00:36:18.817 --> 00:36:20.002
You come here often?

482
00:36:22.885 --> 00:36:24.326
That staff
doesn't belong to you.

483
00:36:28.202 --> 00:36:30.444
You have to give it to me.
or somebody might get hurt.

484
00:36:44.442 --> 00:36:45.369
[grunting]

485
00:36:46.523 --> 00:36:47.420
Yah!

486
00:37:37.292 --> 00:37:38.731
[sipping]

487
00:37:47.957 --> 00:37:50.679
What kind of monk
are you. huh?

488
00:37:50.680 --> 00:37:51.960
Stealing from travelers.

489
00:37:54.523 --> 00:37:55.547
Ah!

490
00:37:55.548 --> 00:37:57.053
A silent one. I see.

491
00:37:58.335 --> 00:37:59.422
Or deaf.

492
00:38:01.923 --> 00:38:03.682
I'm speaking to you. monk!

493
00:38:03.683 --> 00:38:04.323
Hmm?

494
00:38:14.061 --> 00:38:14.765
[Lu groans]

495
00:38:18.161 --> 00:38:18.993
Hey!

496
00:38:27.898 --> 00:38:29.370
[groaning]

497
00:38:35.201 --> 00:38:35.777
Ugh!

498
00:39:13.508 --> 00:39:14.597
[groaning]

499
00:39:38.556 --> 00:39:40.252
Praying Mantis.

500
00:39:40.253 --> 00:39:41.534
Very good...

501
00:39:41.535 --> 00:39:42.624
for catching bugs.

502
00:39:42.625 --> 00:39:43.777
But not tiger!

503
00:40:41.111 --> 00:40:42.231
[groans]

504
00:40:42.232 --> 00:40:44.313
[burping]

505
00:41:12.116 --> 00:41:13.363
Aah!

506
00:41:36.619 --> 00:41:38.539
You tried to steal the staff
for the Warlord!

507
00:41:38.540 --> 00:41:39.563
No. fool!

508
00:41:42.095 --> 00:41:45.010
I'm on a mission to find
the seeker of the staff.

509
00:42:03.203 --> 00:42:04.707
You found him.

510
00:42:18.321 --> 00:42:19.505
[speaking Chinese]

511
00:42:36.002 --> 00:42:37.122
Ah!

512
00:42:53.074 --> 00:42:54.578
[chuckles]

513
00:42:54.579 --> 00:42:55.987
[laughing]

514
00:42:57.205 --> 00:42:59.671
[laughing]

515
00:42:59.672 --> 00:43:01.112
[laughing]

516
00:43:18.666 --> 00:43:20.555
JASON: How long have you been
searching for the staff?

517
00:43:20.556 --> 00:43:22.156
SILENT MONK:
As long as I can remember.

518
00:43:25.553 --> 00:43:26.865
[speaking Chinese]

519
00:43:41.888 --> 00:43:42.783
Aah!

520
00:43:47.588 --> 00:43:48.196
Aah!

521
00:43:58.254 --> 00:43:59.856
[quivering]

522
00:44:32.430 --> 00:44:34.767
Jason. go deeper!

523
00:44:34.768 --> 00:44:37.137
Must taste bitter
before sweet.

524
00:44:37.138 --> 00:44:38.162
Horse stance.
Grow roots.

525
00:44:50.848 --> 00:44:51.679
Horse stance.

526
00:44:53.346 --> 00:44:55.812
Very good...
for taking a dump.

527
00:44:57.350 --> 00:44:58.854
Hey!

528
00:44:58.855 --> 00:45:00.072
Enough from you!

529
00:45:00.073 --> 00:45:02.762
He's my student.
not yours!

530
00:45:02.763 --> 00:45:05.389
Two tigers cannot live
on the same mountain.

531
00:45:05.390 --> 00:45:07.598
Two masters cannot teach
the same student!

532
00:45:10.546 --> 00:45:11.025
<i>Ma Bu!</i>

533
00:45:13.076 --> 00:45:15.894
If he is really
to learn the kung-fu.

534
00:45:15.895 --> 00:45:18.713
he must develop speed.
accuracy. and power.

535
00:45:18.714 --> 00:45:21.564
Hey! I know that.

536
00:45:21.565 --> 00:45:23.260
It's the way
of the intercepting fist.

537
00:45:23.261 --> 00:45:23.806
Bruce Lee?

538
00:45:31.461 --> 00:45:32.807
I will punch.

539
00:45:32.808 --> 00:45:34.024
You block.

540
00:45:34.025 --> 00:45:34.632
Ready?

541
00:45:36.714 --> 00:45:38.603
Ohh!

542
00:45:38.604 --> 00:45:40.077
What did I teach you
about the Snake?

543
00:45:41.487 --> 00:45:42.479
Now you punch me.

544
00:45:44.178 --> 00:45:45.105
[groans]

545
00:45:45.106 --> 00:45:46.226
See?

546
00:45:49.013 --> 00:45:50.391
Again.
You punch him again.

547
00:45:50.392 --> 00:45:51.095
Snake!

548
00:45:53.595 --> 00:45:54.555
[choking]

549
00:45:54.556 --> 00:45:55.612
He's not ready for Snake.

550
00:45:55.613 --> 00:45:57.372
Perhaps Eagle.

551
00:45:57.373 --> 00:45:59.263
Crane! Crane!

552
00:46:00.578 --> 00:46:01.857
Okay?

553
00:46:01.858 --> 00:46:03.234
[Jason grunting
and groaning]

554
00:46:04.805 --> 00:46:05.894
Aah!

555
00:46:07.239 --> 00:46:09.288
Ow! Ow! Ow!

556
00:46:09.289 --> 00:46:11.402
Aah! Oh!

557
00:46:11.403 --> 00:46:13.196
Stop!

558
00:46:13.197 --> 00:46:14.253
I've had enough!

559
00:46:14.253 --> 00:46:15.983
No more!

560
00:46:15.984 --> 00:46:17.552
No more silent riddles!

561
00:46:18.641 --> 00:46:19.665
And no more empty cups!

562
00:46:22.485 --> 00:46:24.662
[grunts]

563
00:46:24.663 --> 00:46:26.488
First. you show respect
to your teachers!

564
00:46:29.756 --> 00:46:32.510
So. what about the two tigers
on one mountain?

565
00:46:34.433 --> 00:46:35.745
We can kill each other
when it's over.

566
00:46:38.244 --> 00:46:40.101
Aah ha ha!

567
00:46:40.102 --> 00:46:41.735
Ha ha ha ha ha!

568
00:46:41.736 --> 00:46:43.656
Ohh!

569
00:46:43.657 --> 00:46:46.218
[Jason groaning]

570
00:46:46.219 --> 00:46:48.044
LU: Kung-fu.

571
00:46:48.045 --> 00:46:50.927
Hard work over time
to accomplish skill.

572
00:46:50.928 --> 00:46:51.760
[Jason groaning]

573
00:46:54.259 --> 00:46:55.635
Aah! Aah!

574
00:46:55.636 --> 00:46:58.005
LU:
A painter can have kung-fu.

575
00:46:58.006 --> 00:46:59.863
[grunting]
Or the butcher who cuts meat

576
00:46:59.864 --> 00:47:04.219
every day with such skill
his knife never touches bone.

577
00:47:04.219 --> 00:47:06.109
[groaning]

578
00:47:08.768 --> 00:47:11.266
SILENT MONK: Learn the form.
but seek the formless.

579
00:47:12.484 --> 00:47:14.726
Hear the soundless.

580
00:47:14.727 --> 00:47:17.961
Learn it all.
then forget it all.

581
00:47:17.962 --> 00:47:21.804
Learn the way.
then find your own way.

582
00:47:22.926 --> 00:47:25.167
LU:
The musician can have kung-fu.

583
00:47:25.168 --> 00:47:28.081
or the poet who paints
pictures with words

584
00:47:28.082 --> 00:47:30.515
and makes emperors weep.

585
00:47:30.516 --> 00:47:33.111
This. too. is kung-fu.

586
00:47:33.112 --> 00:47:35.224
SILENT MONK:
But do not name it. my friend.

587
00:47:35.225 --> 00:47:37.371
for it is like water.

588
00:47:37.372 --> 00:47:39.676
Nothing is softer than water.

589
00:47:39.677 --> 00:47:42.431
yet it can overcome rock.

590
00:47:42.432 --> 00:47:44.161
It does not fight.

591
00:47:44.162 --> 00:47:46.627
It flows around the opponent.

592
00:47:46.628 --> 00:47:48.933
LU: Formless. nameless.

593
00:47:48.934 --> 00:47:51.784
the true master dwells within.

594
00:47:51.785 --> 00:47:53.770
Only you can free him.

595
00:48:40.726 --> 00:48:42.743
[flies buzzing]

596
00:48:51.488 --> 00:48:53.217
[ropes creaking]

597
00:48:54.916 --> 00:48:57.349
SILENT MONK: Behold the tyranny
of the Warlord.

598
00:48:57.350 --> 00:49:00.329
GOLDEN SPARROW:
He must be stopped.

599
00:49:00.329 --> 00:49:03.627
He must be killed for his crimes
and his head put on a post.

600
00:49:04.973 --> 00:49:08.367
But we must not feel hatred
towards him. or he wins.

601
00:49:11.347 --> 00:49:14.517
If he speaks of compassion
for this devil.

602
00:49:14.518 --> 00:49:17.368
he should go back
to his temple and pray.

603
00:49:17.369 --> 00:49:20.186
Our mission
is not one of peace.

604
00:49:20.187 --> 00:49:23.229
Go back
to your mother and father.

605
00:49:23.230 --> 00:49:24.414
You are but a child.

606
00:49:25.888 --> 00:49:26.560
They are dead.

607
00:49:28.739 --> 00:49:30.596
GOLDEN SPARROW:
And she's not a child.

608
00:49:32.679 --> 00:49:33.862
Not anymore.

609
00:49:36.439 --> 00:49:38.296
Her father...

610
00:49:38.297 --> 00:49:41.852
was a government official
who opposed the Warlord.

611
00:49:43.646 --> 00:49:46.497
And so. to set an example.

612
00:49:46.498 --> 00:49:49.411
the Warlord dispatched
his troops into the night.

613
00:49:49.412 --> 00:49:51.590
[sound of soldiers marching]

614
00:49:54.378 --> 00:49:58.317
Legion upon legion poured out
of the Five Elements Mountain

615
00:49:58.318 --> 00:50:01.617
into the lowlands
of the Middle Kingdom.

616
00:50:01.618 --> 00:50:02.834
[people screaming]

617
00:50:02.835 --> 00:50:06.134
Screams of innocent people
hung in the night air.

618
00:50:09.402 --> 00:50:14.719
When it was over. charred ruins
were all that remained.

619
00:50:14.720 --> 00:50:18.563
That. and a lonely child. hidden
in the well by her mother...

620
00:50:19.909 --> 00:50:21.446
ruthlessly murdered
by an arrow...

621
00:50:24.394 --> 00:50:26.251
from the Warlord's bow.

622
00:50:27.790 --> 00:50:30.320
[crying]

623
00:50:31.570 --> 00:50:34.100
When she reaches
the Warlord's palace...

624
00:50:36.022 --> 00:50:38.168
She will
not offer him forgiveness...

625
00:50:39.675 --> 00:50:41.628
monk.

626
00:50:41.629 --> 00:50:43.229
She will offer him...

627
00:50:43.230 --> 00:50:44.255
this...

628
00:50:50.758 --> 00:50:54.025
a Jade dart
that can kill an immortal.

629
00:50:55.404 --> 00:50:57.677
Long has she practiced.

630
00:51:02.963 --> 00:51:05.589
Vengeance has a way
of rebounding upon oneself.

631
00:51:10.747 --> 00:51:11.963
Huh.

632
00:51:11.964 --> 00:51:13.469
Master of Sensitivity.

633
00:51:25.323 --> 00:51:26.476
[speaking Chinese]

634
00:51:41.564 --> 00:51:42.941
[horse whinnying]

635
00:51:49.990 --> 00:51:53.545
[panting]

636
00:51:55.180 --> 00:51:56.588
Damn.

637
00:51:56.589 --> 00:51:57.388
This desert is hot.

638
00:51:59.632 --> 00:52:00.496
This is not a desert.

639
00:52:01.971 --> 00:52:03.796
That is the desert!

640
00:52:08.762 --> 00:52:10.875
LU: I Hope you know
where you're going!

641
00:52:10.876 --> 00:52:11.420
Crazy monk.

642
00:52:23.785 --> 00:52:25.035
Oh!

643
00:53:17.443 --> 00:53:19.973
[wind howling]

644
00:53:26.349 --> 00:53:28.462
A monk on a mission.

645
00:53:28.463 --> 00:53:29.647
And where does he lead us?

646
00:53:29.648 --> 00:53:31.441
Across a desert to nowhere.

647
00:53:56.653 --> 00:53:58.062
We're not gonna make it.
are we?

648
00:54:02.708 --> 00:54:04.469
And even if we do. we still
have to face the Jade Army.

649
00:54:08.058 --> 00:54:09.818
What if I can't handle it?

650
00:54:15.745 --> 00:54:17.058
What if I freeze?

651
00:54:21.991 --> 00:54:23.465
Don't forget to breathe.

652
00:54:56.396 --> 00:54:59.920
If we don't find water soon.
we will perish.

653
00:55:02.131 --> 00:55:05.365
Perhaps a Taoist immortal
can make rain.

654
00:55:07.993 --> 00:55:11.004
If he truly is
a Taoist immortal.

655
00:56:07.706 --> 00:56:08.793
[gagging]

656
00:56:13.663 --> 00:56:14.624
[speaking quietly
in Chinese]

657
00:56:33.653 --> 00:56:35.862
You are an insult
to the name of Buddha!

658
00:56:35.863 --> 00:56:36.631
Blasphemy!

659
00:56:40.316 --> 00:56:40.955
Look!

660
00:56:42.847 --> 00:56:44.383
I lead you to the mountain!

661
00:56:46.562 --> 00:56:47.234
Out there!

662
00:56:57.485 --> 00:56:58.190
[grunting]

663
00:57:22.089 --> 00:57:25.195
[Chinese lute playing]

664
00:57:54.540 --> 00:57:55.050
Can you see them...

665
00:57:56.206 --> 00:57:57.166
in the clouds?

666
00:57:58.319 --> 00:57:59.567
A two-headed lion.

667
00:58:01.138 --> 00:58:02.579
Right there.

668
00:58:02.580 --> 00:58:03.476
See?

669
00:58:05.013 --> 00:58:05.910
Yeah. I see.

670
00:58:07.994 --> 00:58:08.986
See that one?

671
00:58:08.987 --> 00:58:10.138
Right there.
coming up behind it?

672
00:58:11.229 --> 00:58:12.156
Like a wave?

673
00:58:13.887 --> 00:58:15.104
Looks like
the Green Monster.

674
00:58:16.194 --> 00:58:18.019
Green Monster?

675
00:58:18.020 --> 00:58:19.012
You mean dragon.

676
00:58:20.551 --> 00:58:21.671
No. I mean Fenway Park.

677
00:58:22.825 --> 00:58:24.650
They call the left field fence
the Green Monster.

678
00:58:26.541 --> 00:58:27.469
It's true.

679
00:58:30.769 --> 00:58:32.019
It does kind of look like
a dragon. though. doesn't it?

680
00:58:37.048 --> 00:58:40.379
Have you family back
in this land you come from?

681
00:58:42.622 --> 00:58:43.775
My mother.

682
00:58:44.673 --> 00:58:45.697
Father?

683
00:58:47.780 --> 00:58:48.324
Never knew him.

684
00:58:50.663 --> 00:58:52.200
Do you ever long for him?

685
00:58:54.379 --> 00:58:55.724
Wonder who he was?

686
00:58:59.568 --> 00:59:01.778
Maybe the only thing
I've ever been good at...

687
00:59:03.893 --> 00:59:04.917
pretending that I don't.

688
00:59:08.218 --> 00:59:09.562
She is sorry.

689
00:59:14.433 --> 00:59:16.002
NI CHANG: How romantic.

690
00:59:18.276 --> 00:59:21.607
NI CHANG: Men will tell you
what you want to hear. Sparrow.

691
00:59:21.608 --> 00:59:25.067
But in the end. they will
leave you with nothing.

692
00:59:29.008 --> 00:59:31.153
You survived
the River of Sand.

693
00:59:31.154 --> 00:59:32.531
Impressive.

694
00:59:32.532 --> 00:59:34.292
And you. boy...

695
00:59:34.293 --> 00:59:35.895
so far from home.

696
00:59:35.896 --> 00:59:39.418
I can ensure
your safe return.

697
00:59:39.419 --> 00:59:41.340
Just bring
the weapon forward.

698
00:59:41.341 --> 00:59:42.141
I don't think so.

699
00:59:43.583 --> 00:59:44.479
Why do you
want the staff?

700
00:59:46.146 --> 00:59:48.356
When I deliver
the lost weapon.

701
00:59:48.357 --> 00:59:52.104
the Jade Warlord shall grant me
the Elixir of Immortality.

702
00:59:54.572 --> 00:59:57.294
An orphan girl.
a lost traveler.

703
00:59:57.295 --> 01:00:00.433
an old drunk.
and a monk who has failed

704
01:00:00.434 --> 01:00:02.322
at the same task
for half his life.

705
01:00:02.323 --> 01:00:04.438
[scoffs]

706
01:00:04.439 --> 01:00:08.921
Misfits following a misfit
in hopes of rescuing...a misfit.

707
01:00:14.303 --> 01:00:15.072
Oh!

708
01:00:22.921 --> 01:00:23.817
[grunts]

709
01:00:26.253 --> 01:00:26.829
Aah!

710
01:00:29.425 --> 01:00:30.256
Kill them.

711
01:00:30.257 --> 01:00:33.492
[soldiers shouting]

712
01:00:41.438 --> 01:00:42.142
Aah!

713
01:00:44.512 --> 01:00:47.651
[screaming]

714
01:00:55.596 --> 01:00:56.781
Aah!
- Aah!

715
01:01:02.611 --> 01:01:04.597
[grunting]

716
01:01:10.012 --> 01:01:11.420
Wah!

717
01:01:22.217 --> 01:01:22.889
Oh!

718
01:01:22.890 --> 01:01:24.555
[soldiers shouting]

719
01:01:41.566 --> 01:01:42.814
[whip snaps]

720
01:01:42.815 --> 01:01:43.999
LU: Hyah!

721
01:02:25.324 --> 01:02:27.950
Lu! You okay?

722
01:02:27.950 --> 01:02:28.910
Just thirsty.

723
01:02:33.460 --> 01:02:34.485
Lu!

724
01:02:41.918 --> 01:02:43.583
[grunting]

725
01:02:51.367 --> 01:02:53.129
It's okay.
He's immortal. right?

726
01:02:53.130 --> 01:02:54.283
I mean. he is. right?

727
01:02:54.284 --> 01:02:56.461
Wine.
He needs his wine!

728
01:02:56.462 --> 01:02:57.453
There is nothing we can do.

729
01:02:57.454 --> 01:02:58.607
What are you saying?

730
01:02:58.608 --> 01:02:59.407
We have to do something!

731
01:02:59.408 --> 01:03:00.849
[goats bleating]

732
01:03:18.180 --> 01:03:20.134
[monks shouting]

733
01:03:32.148 --> 01:03:35.543
ABBOT: I'm afraid the wound
is too deep.

734
01:03:35.544 --> 01:03:37.047
He will not survive it.

735
01:03:38.618 --> 01:03:39.515
JASON: He needs wine.

736
01:03:40.830 --> 01:03:43.199
He's one of
the eight immortals.

737
01:03:43.200 --> 01:03:44.287
Wine is his Elixir.
Please.

738
01:03:46.979 --> 01:03:48.612
ABBOT:
We will send a walking monk.

739
01:03:49.991 --> 01:03:51.495
LU: Don't you have
a running monk?

740
01:04:13.184 --> 01:04:14.176
When I was your age...

741
01:04:15.330 --> 01:04:17.539
I was a scholar-warrior
in training.

742
01:04:19.237 --> 01:04:21.544
My arrow was good.
So. too. my kung-fu.

743
01:04:22.825 --> 01:04:27.759
So I was chosen to take
the civil examinations.

744
01:04:29.168 --> 01:04:31.058
To pass would place me...

745
01:04:32.500 --> 01:04:35.831
in the very short line
of scholar immortals.

746
01:04:39.452 --> 01:04:40.156
I failed.

747
01:04:42.719 --> 01:04:43.487
You're not an immortal?

748
01:04:46.499 --> 01:04:49.893
If one
does not attach himself

749
01:04:49.894 --> 01:04:51.719
to people and desires...

750
01:04:54.155 --> 01:04:56.365
never shall
his heart be broken.

751
01:04:58.704 --> 01:04:59.568
But then...

752
01:05:01.555 --> 01:05:02.931
does he ever truly live?

753
01:05:06.744 --> 01:05:07.865
I would rather die
a mortal...

754
01:05:10.557 --> 01:05:11.678
who has cared
about someone...

755
01:05:13.920 --> 01:05:16.290
than a man free

756
01:05:16.291 --> 01:05:17.315
from his own death.

757
01:05:19.783 --> 01:05:21.127
I don't want to lose you.

758
01:05:24.268 --> 01:05:25.836
Forget about me.

759
01:05:29.232 --> 01:05:32.339
ABBOT: There is only one
Elixir of Immortality.

760
01:05:32.340 --> 01:05:35.414
It is
the Emperor's mix of Jade.

761
01:05:35.415 --> 01:05:38.490
Cinnabar.
and Salts of Mercury.

762
01:05:38.491 --> 01:05:41.949
It is forever stored in
the realm of the Jade Palace...

763
01:05:43.264 --> 01:05:47.588
high in the Jade firmament.
rarely touched by mortals.

764
01:05:47.589 --> 01:05:51.112
To reach it. one
must take the north road

765
01:05:51.113 --> 01:05:52.073
and cross the border

766
01:05:52.074 --> 01:05:53.321
of heaven and earth...

767
01:05:54.347 --> 01:05:56.942
only to face
the Jade Army.

768
01:05:59.153 --> 01:06:00.113
I'm sorry.

769
01:06:01.203 --> 01:06:02.868
There is no other way.

770
01:06:03.894 --> 01:06:05.463
Yes. there is.

771
01:06:07.001 --> 01:06:09.948
In two nights.
there should be no moon.

772
01:06:09.949 --> 01:06:12.734
We can take the south side
of the fourth peak

773
01:06:12.735 --> 01:06:13.824
under cover of darkness.

774
01:06:15.299 --> 01:06:16.611
We have to go now.
No!

775
01:06:17.733 --> 01:06:18.693
But he's going to die!

776
01:06:20.455 --> 01:06:21.928
We go now. we all die.

777
01:06:26.542 --> 01:06:29.296
There is more at stake.
an entire kingdom.

778
01:06:33.462 --> 01:06:34.901
Your passage home.

779
01:06:37.466 --> 01:06:41.406
We will advance in two nights.
when the moon has ceased.

780
01:06:41.407 --> 01:06:42.719
So be it!

781
01:06:50.984 --> 01:06:53.642
[thunder rumbling
in the distance]

782
01:07:28.336 --> 01:07:28.912
When she met you...

783
01:07:29.938 --> 01:07:32.852
long ago in a tea house...

784
01:07:34.326 --> 01:07:35.991
you were a lost boy
and frightened.

785
01:07:39.740 --> 01:07:41.341
Not the kind
she would stand and fight with.

786
01:09:32.692 --> 01:09:34.647
You've made
a most excellent judgment.

787
01:09:51.913 --> 01:09:53.834
The seeker from the prophecy.

788
01:09:55.309 --> 01:09:57.454
Not quite what I expected.

789
01:09:57.455 --> 01:10:00.882
JASON: A man is dying
back on Song Mountain.

790
01:10:00.883 --> 01:10:02.388
I need the Elixir.

791
01:10:03.862 --> 01:10:06.424
And why should
I give it to you?

792
01:10:06.425 --> 01:10:08.827
Because I brought you
the staff.

793
01:10:08.828 --> 01:10:10.364
The life of your friend

794
01:10:10.365 --> 01:10:12.062
for the power
to rule a kingdom?

795
01:10:13.185 --> 01:10:14.849
A most reasonable offer.

796
01:10:15.907 --> 01:10:18.821
This man. a good friend?

797
01:10:20.071 --> 01:10:21.801
And a good teacher.

798
01:10:21.802 --> 01:10:24.747
The man who honors
his teacher honors himself.

799
01:10:26.158 --> 01:10:29.585
However. there is
a bit of a problem

800
01:10:29.586 --> 01:10:31.474
with your request.

801
01:10:31.475 --> 01:10:33.205
You see...

802
01:10:33.206 --> 01:10:36.505
I've promised the Elixir
to someone else.

803
01:10:36.506 --> 01:10:38.395
But she didn't
bring you the staff.

804
01:10:38.396 --> 01:10:39.900
I did.

805
01:10:39.901 --> 01:10:41.693
The boy has a point.

806
01:10:45.186 --> 01:10:47.844
My liege.
you made a promise.

807
01:10:47.845 --> 01:10:52.456
There is but one way
to resolve such matters.

808
01:10:52.457 --> 01:10:54.987
A martial challenge...
to the death.

809
01:10:57.712 --> 01:10:58.799
With pleasure.

810
01:11:15.139 --> 01:11:16.995
The Elixir of Immortality.

811
01:11:21.417 --> 01:11:24.460
The prize goes to the winner.

812
01:11:57.296 --> 01:11:57.871
Yah!

813
01:12:08.187 --> 01:12:08.666
[groaning]

814
01:12:16.260 --> 01:12:17.124
[groaning]

815
01:12:30.740 --> 01:12:31.444
Aah!

816
01:12:40.285 --> 01:12:41.278
No!

817
01:12:46.917 --> 01:12:48.421
[grunting]

818
01:13:13.344 --> 01:13:14.144
Ahh!

819
01:13:21.674 --> 01:13:22.281
[groaning]

820
01:13:26.126 --> 01:13:27.631
[groaning]

821
01:13:34.487 --> 01:13:35.384
[Jason shouts]

822
01:13:43.297 --> 01:13:44.705
[grunting]

823
